Z||000000||mrfixit58||11-10-1999||09:13 AM||||I've been trying to find out some details about converting my 87 GT to 3800 Series II motor. My GT is an automatic so I am also considering switching the tranny as well to gai overdrive. Other than just companies just advertising a kit, I am looking for more detail.<P>I'm pretty handy with a wrench/tourch/welder and once installed a small block Chevy in a 72 Chevy LUV so I'm confident that I can fabricate everything that is needed. I'm just looking for more details before I start dropping $$$ into the project.<P>If anyone has completed this project and have the instructions leftover, I would love to talk to you.||||reg||5
Z||000002||mrfixit58||11-10-1999||03:49 PM||||terryk,<P>Thanks for responding. You mentioned "Start looking for the trans and engine mounts from a 3.8L A car". What is an "A" car?<P>You also mentioned that passenger side axle would need to be shorter. Unfortunatly, I don't have any experience with CV-joint cars. Can I just have the stock axle shortened (re-splined?)?<P>Finally, you kind of blew me away with the backwards shifter mechanism. Are you refering to the transmission end or the shifter end?<P>Thanks again,||||reg||4
Z||000004||mrfixit58||11-12-1999||08:39 AM||||Sounds like you know your stuff. Thanks for taking the time to answer some of my questions. Based on some of the stuff your telling me, it's hard to imagine a swap "kit" being worth the $1800 that is being asked. Especially when the disclaimers say that it only provide your with "the information necessary" to hook up A/C and "exhaust not included". <P>Asside from the wiring and a few brackets, what's left? It seems to me that some of the more computer literate Fieroites who have completed this swap could post the pictorial brakedown of their project at a web site for other's to see. Something simular to the disc brake upgrade and the home made turbo system that's already out there.<P>Just a thought,<BR>thanks again,<BR>Roy||||reg||14
